// A diamond DAG (DD-12 §12, N27): `bottom` has two parents; the first to
// reach it in the BFS, `left`, keeps it, and `right -> bottom` is drawn
// straight by the host. The tree arcs are elbows (N34). No diagnostic.
@layout: { engine: tree }
top: "Top"
left: "Left"
right: "Right"
bottom: { @label: "Bottom", @shape: diamond }
top -> left
top -> right
left -> bottom
right -> bottom
